 "case": {
  "id": "tp53-lfs",
  "title": "A family with early cancers",
  "brief": "<p><b>Referral from the breast clinic.</b> A woman of 33 had HER2-positive breast cancer at 29. Her brother had an osteosarcoma at 15. Her mother had breast cancer at 36 and died at 39. A maternal aunt had a leiomyosarcoma at 41, and her maternal grandfather died of a glioblastoma at 46.</p><p>Testing with the Li-Fraumeni syndrome panel of <i>TP53</i> and <i>POT1</i> found a heterozygous <i>TP53</i> variant, NM_000546.6:c.818G&gt;A p.(Arg273His). Since then her brother and her maternal aunt have been tested, and both carry it. Her maternal uncle, who is well at 55, does not carry it. Her sister, who is well at 30, has not been tested.</p>",
  "tasks": [
   "Open the variant and go through its evidence: its frequency, the predictions, the protein, ClinVar and the literature. Is codon 273 a hotspot?",
   "Check the relatives’ genotypes on the Family tab, then use the segregation calculator on the variant’s page. Is PP1 met, and if so, at what strength?",
   "Classify the variant and sign it, then compare your criteria with the ClinGen TP53 expert panel’s.",
   "Write the report. What would you offer her sister?"
  ],
  "source": "The variant is NM_000546.6(TP53):c.818G>A (GRCh38 17-7673802-C-T, ClinGen allele CA000434). The sources are ClinVar VCV000012366 and the ClinGen TP53 VCEP’s classification in the Evidence Repository, checked in October 2026. The patient and family are fictional."
 },
