    "source": "ClinGen TP53 expert panel (VCEP), Evidence Repository, specifications v2.0.0; ClinVar VCV000012366 (Pathogenic, reviewed by expert panel, 2024-08-05). PP1 is based on this family’s results.",
    "notes": {
     "PS4": "Met at a very strong level, because the variant has been reported in many unrelated people who meet the classic Li-Fraumeni or revised Chompret criteria. Together they add up to 8 phenotype points by the TP53 VCEP’s scoring.",
     "PS2": "Met from the literature. The variant has been seen de novo, with parentage confirmed, in a person with a Li-Fraumeni cancer, who scores 4 phenotype points. This patient’s variant is not de novo.",
     "PS3": "Met, because transactivation assays in yeast and human cells show that the protein does not work and does not suppress growth.",
     "PM1": "Codon 273 is one of the mutational hotspots the TP53 VCEP lists.",
     "PM2": "Met at supporting strength, because the variant’s frequency is below the VCEP’s thresholds. These are 0.003% overall and 0.004% in any group with more than one allele, leaving out founder groups such as Ashkenazi Jewish people. In gnomAD v4.1 the variant is at 1.1 in 100,000 alleles overall and 1.2 in 100,000 European alleles.",
     "PP3": "Met, because the BayesDel score of 0.52 and the Align-GVGD class of C25 are both above the VCEP’s thresholds.",
     "PP4": "Met at moderate strength under one of the TP53 VCEP’s rules, because the variant has been found at a variant allele fraction of 5 to 25% in at least two people.",
     "PP1": "Met at supporting strength from this family, because both affected relatives who were tested carry the variant and the unaffected uncle does not. The likelihood ratio is about 14, the equivalent of just under 4 informative meioses. Like the ACGS, the TP53 panel counts meioses. It treats 3 to 4 as supporting, 5 to 6 as moderate, and 7 or more across more than one family as strong. By Tavtigian’s odds it would be moderate.",
     "PM5": "Not met, because the VCEP had not curated the five other missense changes at codon 273 that are in ClinVar."
    }
   }
